//? Title: Support Vector Machines: Hinge Loss and Random Features
//? Subtitle: A finite Fourier feature map approximates an RBF kernel
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A classifier can seek a decision boundary with a margin rather than fit class probabilities.
We inspect hinge-loss regions, fit a tiny linear margin model and check the Gaussian-kernel
approximation supplied by random Fourier features. The finite-feature primal model is distinct
from an exact kernel dual, and neither its margins nor its votes are probabilities.
)
\toc

> The method

For labels y in {-1,1} and score f=xᵀw+b, the regularised primal objective is

$$
J(w,b)=\frac1N\sum_i\max(0,1-y_i f(x_i))+\frac\lambda2\|w\|^2.
$$
\alttext(The mean hinge penalty is zero at margins at least one; a squared weight penalty controls the tradeoff.)

The bias is unpenalised. Misclassification (margin <=0) differs from margin violation (margin<1).
At the hinge kink a valid subgradient is used. For nonlinear decisions, concatenate cosine and
sine features with Gaussian frequencies B and divide by sqrt(m). With
B_ij distributed N(0,gamma/(2 pi²)), their expected inner product is exp(-gamma||x-x'||²).
This follows from the characteristic function of a Gaussian. A finite draw approximates the
kernel and may deviate; training a linear margin model on it solves a finite-feature problem.
Feature evaluation costs O(NDm), and primal steps O(Nm).

The concept diagram has a retained TikZ source in `diagrams/support_vector_machines_concept.tikz`.
Regeneration requires LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, and dvisvgm.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/support_vector_machines_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/support_vector_machines_concept.tikz > build/support_vector_machines_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/support_vector_machines_concept.svg build/support_vector_machines_concept.dvi > build/support_vector_machines_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered build/support_vector_machines_concept.svg from local TikZ source.\n'
```
